## Trace contract

List all owned queues and their payload formatters. Define any module duration slices or dependency flows, including their start/end cycle events. State whether every-cycle capture is required or an explicit sampling interval is acceptable.

## Tests

List tests for normal flow, blocked cycles, reset, hierarchy, and log/report output.

## Parallel execution and generated functions

Keep ordinary functions as ordinary calls; do not create queue ports for function
arguments. Generate only actual optional ports and bind non-null endpoints in the
constructor. `PURE static` functions receive explicit const inputs and return
results without queue access. Evaluate current state into pending state in
`Work()` and commit it in `Xfer()`; reset both. A blocked local helper returns to
`Work()`, which must still call `WorkChildren()` exactly once. Keep all five
lifecycle methods and the child/queue helper positions shown in the code template.

Document the selected parallel parent, queue owners, and any Xfer ordering
dependency. Its direct child subtrees run on fixed workers; all other traversal
stays sequential. Do not inspect a different worker's advancing queues in Xfer.
Describe payload ownership after handoff and obey the restricted parallel queue
API in `docs/API/SimQueue.md`. No runtime port or hierarchy changes are allowed.
